{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionHookProductBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionHookProductBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.dimIrrep_eq_numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.dimIrrep_eq_numSYT","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L159-L167","doc":"**Bridge (1) of the `burnside` reduction roadmap.** The hook-length-formula\ndimension of a custom partition is the genuine standard-tableau count of its\ndiagram — the `ℕ` division in `dimIrrep` is exact, since `hookProduct ∣ n!`\nwitnessed by `numSYT_mul_hookProduct_partition`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L153-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_mul_hookProduct_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_mul_hookProduct_partition","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L148-L151","doc":"**Frame–Robinson–Thrall for the custom `Partition n`**: `#SYT · ∏hooks = n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_eq_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_eq_cell","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L142-L146","doc":"The custom list hook product is the cell-based hook product of the associated diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.card_toYoungDiagram'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.card_toYoungDiagram'","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L136-L140","doc":"`YoungDiagram.card` form of `card_toYoungDiagram` — `YoungDiagram.card` is by\ndefinition `cells.card`, but `rw` needs the syntactic form the FRT statement uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.card_toYoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.card_toYoungDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L130-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rowLens_toYoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rowLens_toYoungDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L126-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.toYoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.toYoungDiagram","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L122-L124","doc":"The `YoungDiagram` of a custom `Partition n` (its parts are its row lengths). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_eq_prodHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookProduct_eq_prodHooks","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L100-L118","doc":"**Bridge (1b).** The custom list-based `Partition.hookProduct` equals the corpus\nlist `IdentityI.prodHooks` of the same parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hookLength_eq_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hookLength_eq_term","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L78-L96","doc":"For a genuine cell `(i,j)` the custom hook length equals the corpus list term\n`(rowLen − j) + (colLen j − i) − 1`. Both `rowLen − j` and `colLen j − i` are `≥ 1`\non a cell, so the `ℕ` subtractions are exact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.legLength_eq_colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.legLength_eq_colLen","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L69-L74","doc":"The custom `legLength` in terms of `colLen`: the rows strictly below `i` holding a\ncell in column `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.colLen_drop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.colLen_drop","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L53-L67","doc":"Dropping `k` rows removes exactly `k` cells from every column, because a\nweakly-decreasing `l` has each column's cells in a prefix of the rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.foldl_mul_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.foldl_mul_map","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionHookProductBridge.lean#L43-L49","doc":"A multiplicative `foldl` with an accumulator is the accumulator times the mapped product. ","signatureChunk":0}]}